# The closure-evidence ledger is append-only and now tracked, so two branches
# that each close an issue append a line at the same offset and CONFLICT on
# merge every time. That is not a rare case here: two agent sessions sharing one
# checkout is normal practice in this fleet (feedback_parallel_sessions_one_checkout),
# and a conflict is worse than annoying -- read_receipts() in
# test-updater-issue-sequence.py records any non-JSON line as ledger DAMAGE and
# refuses to skip it, so leftover conflict markers fail the required `validate`
# check hard.
#
# merge=union keeps BOTH sides' lines, which is the correct semantics for an
# append-only ledger: no receipt is ever meant to replace another. Safe here --
# assert_archive_fidelity only refuses on export-ignore/export-subst, not merge.
#
# Found by adversarial review 2026-07-26, before it bit.
.prd-os/receipts.jsonl merge=union
